{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.p4_universality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.p4_universality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.p4_universality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.p4_universality","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L58-L69","doc":"**Universality of the critical exponent** ([`prop:universality`]).\n\nThe critical exponent is **independent of the initial data**: any two\ninitial data yield the same exponent.  *Derived* from\n`alpha_factors_through_invariants` (the exponent factors through the\ncategorical invariants), so the theorem proves universality rather than\nasserting it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:universality","label":"prop:universality","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/p4-universality.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.alpha_factors_through_invariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.alpha_factors_through_invariants","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L55-L55","doc":"**Universality input (Yekutieli tower).** The exponent factors\nthrough the categorical invariants: a map from invariants to the\nexponent value reproduces `α` for every initial datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.invariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.invariants","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The categorical invariants of `(C, A, τ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.α","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.α","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The critical exponent as a function of the initial data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.Exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.Exponent","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The type in which the critical exponent takes its value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.Invariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.Invariants","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The categorical invariants `(χ(A), d, gauge rank)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.InitialData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.InitialData","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Initial data `v₀` of the `q`-NS flow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.P4UniversalityContext","kind":"class","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/p4_universality.lean#L32-L56","doc":"Hypotheses for universality of the critical exponent (§7c: generic\ntypes, no `ℝ`).\n\nThe hypothesis `alpha_factors_through_invariants` packages the\nYekutieli-tower argument: the exponent `α` factors through the\ncategorical invariants — there is a map `f : Invariants → Exponent`\nwith `α v₀ = f invariants` for *every* initial datum `v₀`.  The\nuniversality theorem derives initial-data independence from this; the\nconclusion is not carried as a class field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}